ride:
And on wild clouds of thought, naked together
They ride above us in extreme delight;
We see them, we look up with a lone envy

rides:
Must melt down golden pieces in the nard
Wherewith to anoint her broomstick ere she rides;
And poets evermore are scant of gold,

I sit with her all day
And ride out when she rides.
She sings to me and makes me sing;
